posts=[x for x in calendar if x['activity']=='Publish']
scripts=[]
for i,p in enumerate(posts[:10]):
 beats=[]
 start=0
 treatment=creative[i]
 for end,lines,visual,text,camera,edit,audio in filming[i]:
  dialogue=[dict(speaker=role,line=line) for role,line in lines]
  beats.append(dict(start=start,end=end,dialogue=dialogue,spoken='\n'.join(f"{role}: {line}" for role,line in lines),visual=visual,text=text,camera=camera,edit=edit,audio=audio))
  start=end
 p['hook']=' '.join(d['line'] for d in beats[0]['dialogue'])
 p['format']=treatment['format']
 p['caption']=treatment['caption']
 p['cta']=treatment['cta']
 scripts.append(dict(number=i+1,day=p['day'],date=p['date'],title=p['title'],hook=p['hook'],speaker=treatment['cast'],cast=treatment['cast'],concept=treatment['concept'],purpose=treatment['purpose'],props=treatment['props'],setup=treatment['setup'],format=treatment['format'],length=f"About {start} seconds",duration=start,word_count=sum(len(d['line'].split()) for b in beats for d in b['dialogue']),script='\n\n'.join(b['spoken'] for b in beats),scenes='\n'.join(f"{b['start']}–{b['end']}s: {b['visual']} Camera: {b['camera']} Edit: {b['edit']}" for b in beats),text='\n'.join(f"{b['start']}–{b['end']}s: {b['text']}" for b in beats),beats=beats,caption=p['caption'],hashtags=p['hashtags'],cta=p['cta']))
data=dict(calendar=calendar,scripts=scripts)
(ROOT/'content.js').write_text('window.PROFITLANE_CONTENT = '+json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+';\n')
with (ROOT/'content-calendar.csv').open('w',newline='') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(calendar[0]),lineterminator="\n"); w.writeheader(); w.writerows(calendar)
intro='# 30-day TikTok content calendar\n\nSuggested window: November 9–December 8, 2026. Publish three times weekly: 13 publishing slots. The other 17 days are production, response and review days with reserve concepts, not extra daily posts. Draft audience: independent dispatchers first; independent operators starting their own dispatching second. Goals: brand awareness and attracting potential customers. Tone: educational, professional, casual and relatable. All topics are plans; load examples are fictional. Dates remain suggested and can be shifted. The historical research and exact stakeholder responses are unchanged. Suggested publishing test: 6 p.m. in the audience’s primary time zone; validate through account analytics. See the CSV for spreadsheet use.\n\n'
for p in calendar:
 intro+=f"## Day {p['day']} · {p['date']} · {p['activity']}\n\n"
 for k,label in [('title','Video topic / reserve idea'),('category','Pillar'),('hook','Hook'),('format','Format'),('message','Main message'),('caption','Caption'),('hashtags','Hashtags'),('cta','CTA')]: intro+=f"- **{label}:** {p[k]}\n"
 if p['activity']!='Publish': intro+='- **Work today:** Prepare this reserve concept, respond to relevant comments, or review equal-window results. Do not publish an extra video by default.\n'
 intro+='\n'
(ROOT/'content-calendar.md').write_text(intro.rstrip()+'\n')
s="""# First ten TikTok videos · creative filming scripts

## Start here

These are complete draft scripts with role-labeled dialogue and timed storyboards. **SAY** contains the words to record; read only your role's lines. Camera, action, edit, sound and overlay instructions are not spoken. A helper can film and play multiple roles in separate takes. Timecodes are elapsed minutes:seconds and are planned edit timings, not measured footage. Rehearse at a natural pace and adjust boundaries without rushing; countdowns and reveals include short visual holds.

Angel speaks in videos **1, 4, 6 and 10**, including a founder conversation in 4. These are draft lines for his approval, grounded in his stated vision, not verbatim historical quotes or invented personal experiences. He is a client-to-client speaker, not an influencer character. Videos **2 and 7** are fictional dispatcher–broker role-plays. Videos **3, 6 and 8** use viewer challenges or comparisons. Video **5** is a hands-on fuel demonstration. Video **9** is a clearly labeled paper concept walkthrough. Categories intentionally overlap; each has a different visual engine.

## Small-business production kit

A phone, inexpensive stand or stack of books, window light, quiet desk, paper, marker, calculator and a helper are enough. A toy truck can be a folded paper arrow. Draw schematic routes rather than sourcing map footage. Use a basic phone editor for split screens, freeze frames and simple counters; each storyboard also works with physical paper reveals and straight cuts. No premium animation, second camera or working product screen is required. Film one angle, move the phone, then record the insert. Get a clean take of each dialogue side before assembling the scene.

Use the existing brand assets unchanged: charcoal #2B2F33, amber #F5A623, off-white #F7F5F0 and approved white artwork. Use Barlow Condensed for headings and Barlow for body text, with brand fallbacks. Put charcoal text on off-white/amber; use off-white/amber on charcoal. Avoid small amber text on off-white. Keep logos proportionate and overlays inside TikTok's safe area. Subtitles follow the dialogue; overlays highlight the idea and should appear only at the named reveal.

Shoot stationary in vertical 9:16. No filming while driving. Original footage of a stationary toy/desk is enough; any real trucking B-roll must be safe, original or properly licensed and contain no identifying customer data. Use clean voice audio and quiet licensed music only where it does not hide speech. No strobe effects or copied competitor footage.

Keep **FICTIONAL ROLE-PLAY / HYPOTHETICAL INPUTS** labels throughout the applicable video, and **CONCEPT / IN DEVELOPMENT** labels throughout concept demonstrations. Any score is an arbitrary illustration, never validated or a profitability guarantee. Do not create plausible-looking real product screens, AI scans, company flags, customer testimonials or successful booking outcomes. Independent dispatchers remain primary; independent operators starting their own dispatching are secondary. Product exploration/demo CTAs wait for an approved real route. The four research entries and exact stakeholder responses remain unchanged.

## Video index and format balance

"""
for p in scripts:
 s+=f"{p['number']}. **{p['title']}** — {p['format']} · {p['length']}\n"
s+='\n'
def timestamp(seconds):return f"{seconds//60:02d}:{seconds%60:02d}"
for p in scripts:
 s+=f"## {p['number']}. {p['title']}\n\n**Draft slot:** Day {p['day']} · {p['date']}\n\n**Target length:** {p['length']} · {p['word_count']} spoken words plus visual holds\n\n**Creative concept:** {p['concept']}\n\n**Purpose:** {p['purpose']}\n\n**Who appears / roles:** {p['cast']}\n\n**Props / materials:** {p['props']}\n\n**Low-budget setup:** {p['setup']}\n\n**Opening hook:** {p['hook']}\n\n"
 for b in p['beats']:
  s+=f"### {timestamp(b['start'])}–{timestamp(b['end'])}\n\n**SAY**\n\n"
  for d in b['dialogue']:s+=f"> **{d['speaker']}:** {d['line']}\n\n"
  s+=f"**SHOW / ACTION:** {b['visual']}\n\n**CAMERA / ANGLE:** {b['camera']}\n\n**TRANSITION / GRAPHICS:** {b['edit']}\n\n**ON-SCREEN TEXT:** {b['text']}\n\n**SOUND / DELIVERY:** {b['audio']}\n\n"
 s+=f"**Caption:** {p['caption']}\n\n**Hashtags:** {p['hashtags']}\n\n**Natural CTA / production condition:** {p['cta']}\n\n---\n\n"
(ROOT/'video-scripts.md').write_text(s.rstrip()+'\n')
print('Created 30 calendar entries and 10 distinct creative filming scripts.')
